From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:26:30 -0600
Subject: feat(web): ask for readwrite access by mode, not read

The permission helpers only ever asked about 'read', so a handle the page kept
to write into later, such as one from showSaveFilePicker() that an app stores
to resume an interrupted save, could not be checked or renewed, and
createWritable() threw NotAllowedError after a reload.

FilePermissionMode names the two modes the browser's permission methods take.
hasAccess() and requestAccess() on WebPlatformFile take one, defaulting to
read, so a persisted file is still checked as before. hasPermission() and
requestPermission() take it for a bare handle that is not a WebPlatformFile.

Checked on this commit (the series tip, on 7b8aec33) with Flutter 3.47.9,
Dart 3.13.7 and Chrome 157.0.8103.50:

- `flutter pub get && flutter analyze` in packages/file_picker_web:
  No issues found!
- `flutter test --platform chrome test/web_file_system_access_test.dart`:
  18 passed (dialog choice and fallback, handle store round trip, both
  permission modes, WebPlatformFile read and write paths).
- `flutter test --platform chrome` for the whole package: 67 passed.

Not run: the Android, iOS and desktop suites; the change is web-only.

The two commits can be reviewed in order or squashed; this one builds on the
API the previous one adds.

